      "content": "# B\"H\n\n# Merkava Native Runtime Reality Map\n\nThis file is intentionally blunt. It prevents the native browser from pretending\nto be complete before it is complete.\n\n## Proven now\n\n- `merkavaapp.exe` is a real Windows executable.\n- It loads `.merkava` bytecode headers.\n- It creates a real Win32 OpenGL context.\n- It draws native OpenGL smoke geometry.\n- It accepts basic CLI flags:\n  - `--help`\n  - `--version`\n  - `--check file.js`\n  - `--check file.html`\n  - `--check file.merkava`\n- It analyzes JS/HTML surfaces.\n- It refuses to fake unsupported native Node APIs.\n\n## Not complete yet\n\n- Full native JavaScript VM in C.\n- Full Node.js compatibility.\n- Native CommonJS/ESM module loader.\n- Native HTTP/HTTPS server sockets.\n- Native crypto.\n- Complete native fs semantics.\n- Complete DOM tree/layout/style engine.\n- Complete WebGL API mapped to OpenGL.\n- Full browser event loop/input/paint lifecycle.\n\n## Required architecture\n\n```text\nmerkavaapp.exe\n  -> CLI parser\n  -> runtime mode detector\n  -> Merkava bytecode loader\n  -> native JS VM\n  -> native module loader\n  -> native Node core APIs\n  -> native DOM/CSSOM\n  -> WebGL API table\n  -> OpenGL backend\n  -> browser event loop\n```\n\n## Rule\n\nEvery new claim must have an executable test beside it.\n",
